; supplies.eval — food, water, and what an empty meter does.
;
; Run:  Dungeon.exe -eval tools\EvalScripts\supplies.eval
;
; A MEASUREMENT, not a pass/fail. What a reader is looking for:
;
;   1. WATER RUNS OUT FIRST and bites harder. Both meters drain by time and by
;      exertion, and water is the heavier on both counts — thirst is meant to be
;      what kills you, so if food ever empties first the knobs are wrong.
;   2. CONDITIONING HAS A PRICE. A fitter member burns more food and water per
;      second. Every other loop in this design compounds upward; this is the one
;      that taxes the compounding, so it is the one to watch.
;   3. AN EMPTY METER KILLS (Michael's call). Starving/parched are ordinary
;      effects dealing an ordinary Tick, so they go through the one damage
;      pipeline — which means a tick on a DOWNED member is lethal under the
;      existing overkill rule, with no separate death path written.

logecho on
reset

timescale 0
lockstep on
seed 7
arena open 9 9

echo === 1. a fresh party, and how long its supplies last ===
supplies

echo === 2. conditioning's price ===
; Brand is trained hard and Tilo left untrained. Their `h` columns are the
; measurement: the fitter member should run out SOONER on both meters, at the
; same level, which is the brake the whole design rests on.
setskill 0 conditioning 25
setskill 3 conditioning 0
supplies

echo === 3. an hour of standing still ===
step 3600
supplies

echo === 4. exertion costs supplies, and water more than food ===
; Marching spends stamina, and every stamina point spent bills both meters.
; Compare the DROP in each: water should fall further for the same effort.
setsupply all food 50
setsupply all water 50
echo --- before the march ---
supplies
forward 8
step 20
echo --- after eight steps ---
supplies

echo === 5. an empty meter kills ===
; Water first, since that is the one a real run meets. The effect should appear,
; bite every frame, and lift the moment the member drinks.
setsupply 0 water 0
step 1
echo --- parched ---
supplies
party
char 0
step 20
echo --- twenty seconds of it ---
party
supplies

echo === 6. drinking is the cure ===
; `consume` runs the same DungeonWorld::ConsumeItem the hand menu's drink verb
; does. The effect must lift on the NEXT tick, from the supply tick that owns
; that transition — not from the consume itself, so there is one place a member
; can stop being parched.
consume waterskin 0
supplies
step 1
echo --- after one tick ---
supplies
party
; And the two refusals. A rock feeds nobody; and a member already at maximum
; gains nothing, which must REFUSE rather than consume the item for no effect —
; losing the last waterskin to a full stomach is the kind of thing a player
; never forgives and never notices happening.
consume iron_key 0
setsupply 0 water 100
consume waterskin 0

echo === 7. the meters ride the save (v25) ===
; A new field that does not round-trip is a bug that only shows up hours later,
; on someone else's machine. Set two members to distinctive levels, save, wreck
; them, reload, and read them back.
setsupply 1 food 37
setsupply 2 water 12
save supplytest
setsupply all food 5
setsupply all water 5
echo --- wrecked, before the reload ---
supplies
load supplytest
echo --- reloaded: 37 food on Sera, 12 water on Maren ---
supplies
state
